## 5. Public Package Contract

Users import `chart()` from `ggaction` and import this package to register its
extension actions.

```javascript
import { chart } from "ggaction";
import "{{packageName}}";

const program = chart();
```

Importing `{{packageName}}` must call the public `registerExtension()` API from
`ggaction/extension`. After registration, every program created by `chart()`
includes the extension actions defined by this specification.

Multiple extension packages may be imported together.

```javascript
import { chart } from "ggaction";
import "ggaction-geo";
import "ggaction-hierarchy";

const program = chart()
  .createGeoPlot({})
  .createTreeLayout({});
```

The package must:

- register only the public actions defined in its feature specifications;
- augment the public `ChartProgram` TypeScript type with those actions;
- use `ggaction` as a compatible peer dependency;
- preserve all existing ggaction actions;
- reject extension or action-name collisions before registering any action; and
- avoid depending on extension import order.

The package does not export its own `chart()` function and does not recreate or
wrap ggaction renderers. Rendering continues to use the existing public
ggaction renderer entries.

